# Tour of Garbuix [calc]

/*
A miscellanous example showing some features

- On the left hand side (here) you have a resizable, editable text field where you can write a simplified form of the dot language used by Graphviz, while on the right 👉 you will find the rendered Graphviz, scrollable and zoomable. Not downloadable yet though.
- The first line becomes the title of the diagram.
- Adding [calc] at the end enables operations. More below.
- The replacement directive $DARK modifies all colours to use a Solarized-like style
- The replacement directive on the line below replaces the default color used for the title by the orange defined in Solarized DARK
- The next is how a replacement can look like. Particularly useful if you define certain nodes as "headers"
- The syntax of a node is "NodeInOneWord optionally label with spaces ; graphviz properties". If no label is provided, the NodeInOneWord word will be used
- The syntax of an edge is "NodeInOneWord - > AnotherNode potential text for the edge ; graphviz properties". With no spaces for the arrow, I can't write it like that here. If no label is provided, none will be used.
- You can create clusters as shown, the label will be implied. Optionally add a label or set it as the empty string to remove. Clusters inherit the title font color, size and family.
- You can create tasks. Checking and unchecking should modify the source. It always seems to do it, but it is brittle.
- When using operations like these you always need to define the name of the node, it can't be implied.
- Clusters get an invisible node with the name of the cluster. It can be sometimes useful for anchoring internal nodes, or adding an arrow from a cluster to another.
- If you want to create a fully invisible edge (useful when battling positioning with anchors like those in a cluster) name it !, like in the tasklist cluster
 You can recover this example by pressing `Cmd p` and choosing the obvious option. The other one is for fun (turn on volume and type)
*/

$DARK
$TITLEFONTCOLOR=$ORANGE
$EXAMPLEREPLACEMENT=color="$GREEN" fontcolor="$RED" style="rounded, dashed" penwidth=3

A -> B

B Another node

B -> C named edge

D Links work\nand get a cute\n emoji ; URL="https://github.com/rberenguel"
A -> D ; style="dotted"

cluster tasklist {
  rankdir="LR"
  label="Checkboxes\nin a cluster"
  finishGarbuix [ ] Finish this
  worldDomination [ ] World domination
  finishGarbuix -> worldDomination maybe? ; style="dashed"
  worldDomination -> tasklist ! ; minlen=1
}

cluster operations {
    label="Example operations"
    +_result Result
    Cost1 -> +_result 4
    Cost2 -> +_result 5
    x -> &&_z 90%
    y -> &&_z 30%
    &&_z And? ; $EXAMPLEREPLACEMENT
    *=_Heads2 Heads2
    Heads1 -> *=_Heads2 50% ; minlen=1
    *=_Heads2 -> .=_Result 50% ; minlen=1
    .=_Result Result
    {
       rank=same
       x
       Heads1
       Cost2
       operations
    }
    operations -> x ! ; minlen=1
    Cost2 -> operations ! ; minlen=1
}

tasklist -> operations